'\" t
.\" icli(1) -- IDA Pro command-line interface.
.TH ICLI 1 2026-10-20 "IDA Pro 9.4" "IDA Pro Manual"
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH NAME
icli \- IDA Pro command\-line interface: non-interactive binary analysis, decompilation and annotation
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY icli
.RI [ global-options ]
.I command
.RI [ command-options ]
.RI [ target ]
.RI [ selector ...]
.YS
.SY icli
.B do
.RI [ global-options ]
.I target
.B \-\-
.I step
.RB [ :: " " \fIstep\fR ]...
.YS
.SY icli
.B identify
.RI [ options ]
.IR file ...
.YS
.SY icli
.B diff
.RI [ options ]
.I old new
.YS
.SY icli
.B exec
.RI [ options ]
.I target
.RB [ \-c
.IR code | file | \fB\-\fP ]
.YS
.SY icli
.B ref
.I query
.YS
.SY icli
.B help
.RI [ command | topic ]
.YS
.PP
Commands, by group:
.PP
.TS
l lx.
triage	T{
identify, info, loaders, processors
T}
analysis	T{
analyze, status
T}
query	T{
list, show, disasm, decompile, xrefs, callgraph, search, resolve
T}
edit	T{
rename, comment, type, func, make, patch, tag
T}
journal	T{
apply, log, undo
T}
knowledge	T{
sig, til, lumina, load
T}
output	T{
export
T}
compare	T{
diff, port
T}
automation	T{
do, batch, exec, ref, assert
T}
dynamic	T{
debug, trace
T}
storage	T{
db, cache, vault, serve
T}
meta	T{
config, schema, completion, legacy, help
T}
.TE
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B icli
exposes the IDA kernel, the Hex\-Rays decompilers, the type system, FLIRT,
Lumina, IDA Teams and the debugger as small, composable commands that never
open a window, never ask a question and never wait for a keystroke.
Instructions come from the command line (and optionally standard input);
results go to standard output; diagnostics go to standard error; every
invocation ends with a documented exit status.
.PP
.B icli
is built on idalib and is intended for shell pipelines, Makefiles, CI jobs
and batch processing.
For interactive text\-mode use, see
.BR idat (1).
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH CONCEPTS
.SS Targets
A
.I target
names the database a command operates on.
It may be:
.TP 4
.I a database
.RI ( app.i64 ;
a legacy
.I .idb
is upgraded on first write, see
.BR "db upgrade" ).
.TP
.I an input file
.RI ( app.exe ", " libc.so.6 ", " fw.bin ", " classes.dex ).
.B icli
looks up the cached database for that input (see
.BR "Database cache" )
and creates it on demand.
.TP
.I a container member
.IB container :: member
selects one member of a multi\-image input without extracting it:
.IR app.apk::classes2.dex ,
.IR dyld_shared_cache_arm64e::libsystem_kernel.dylib ,
.IR Foo.app/Contents/MacOS/Foo::arm64
(fat slice),
.IR firmware.zip::rootfs/bin/busybox .
.TP
.I a remote database
.BI vault:// site / path [@ rev ]
checks a database out of an IDA Teams server (credentials from
.BR VAULT_* ,
see
.BR ENVIRONMENT ).
.TP
.I a handle
.BI @ name
registered with
.BR "db tag" ,
or a bare
.B @
meaning \(lqthe target of the previous
.B icli
command in this shell\(rq.
.PP
With no target,
.B icli
uses
.BR $ICLI_DB ,
then the only
.I .i64
in the current directory, and otherwise fails with status 2.
.SS Database cache
When the target is an input file and
.B \-\-db
is not given, the database lives at
.IR $ICLI_CACHE_DIR/ xx / key .i64 ,
where
.I key
is a hash of the input's SHA\-256, every load option, and the kernel
version.
Re\-running any command on an unchanged input reuses the analysed database;
changing one byte, or one load option, yields a new one.
.B \-\-db
.I path
pins the location (to share it or keep it in a project);
.B \-\-no\-cache
analyses into a temporary database discarded on exit.
.SS Analysis lifecycle
A database moves monotonically through four states, reported by
.BR "icli status" :
.TP 12
.B loaded
The loader has mapped segments, applied fixups, created entries, imports
and exports.
No auto\-analysis has run.
.TP
.B analyzing
Auto\-analysis queues are not empty (interrupted, or stopped by
.BR \-\-analysis\-timeout ).
.TP
.B analyzed
All queues are empty, including FLIRT, type library application and the
final pass
.RB ( auto_is_ok ()
in SDK terms).
.TP
.B enriched
Optional passes requested with
.B analyze \-\-with
(Lumina, PDB/DWARF, RTTI, language metadata, whole\-program decompilation)
have completed.
.PP
Every command declares the minimum state it needs and
.B icli
catches up first, printing progress on standard error.
That is what makes
.B "icli decompile ./a.out main"
a valid first command on a never\-seen file.
.B \-\-analysis
.BR auto | none | wait
controls this (see
.BR "GLOBAL OPTIONS" ).
.SS Selections
Most commands take one or more
.IR selectors :
expressions denoting a set of addresses, ranges, functions, names, strings,
types or diff records.
Several selectors are a union.
A selector of
.B \-
reads selectors from standard input, one per line; JSON objects with an
.BR ea ,
.BR start ,
.B from
or
.B to
field are accepted, so the output of one
.B icli
command feeds the next.
The full grammar is in
.BR SELECTORS .
.SS Fields
Every object
.B icli
knows about has named
.IR fields :
.BR ea ,
.BR name ,
.BR size ,
.BR xrefs_to ,
.BR cyclomatic ,
.BR pseudocode ,
\&...
The same names are used as
.IP \(bu 2
keys of
.BR json / jsonl / csv
records,
.IP \(bu
variables in selector predicates:
.BR "func:*[size > 0x400 && xrefs_to >= 10]" ,
.IP \(bu
placeholders in text templates:
.BR "\-t \(aq{ea}  {size:>8}  {name}\(aq" ,
.IP \(bu
placeholders in edit arguments:
.BR "rename app.exe dummy \(aqf_{hash:.8}\(aq" ,
.IP \(bu
placeholders in output paths:
.BR "\-o \(aqsrc/{name}.c\(aq" .
.PP
See
.BR "FIELDS AND TEMPLATES" .
.SS The journal
Edit commands are declarative: they state the desired end state.
.B "icli rename app.exe 0x401000 parse_header"
exits 0 whether or not the name was already
.IR parse_header ,
and reports
.B unchanged
in the latter case.
Each effective change is appended to a journal stored inside the database
(netnode
.BR $icli.journal ),
so it travels with the file and through IDA Teams.
Records carry revision, time, author, command, and before/after values.
.BR log ,
.B undo
and
.B apply
read, revert and replay it.
.SS Chains
.B icli do
opens one database and runs a sequence of steps against it, strictly left
to right, separated by
.BR :: .
Each step is an ordinary command with its target omitted.
Selections and settings never leak between steps unless stated with
.B \-\-keep\-selection
(the result of the previous step becomes the selector
.BR % ).
Chains may be stored as
.I recipes
and invoked as
.BI @ name
(see
.BR "icli do" ).
.SS Python
Anything the commands do not cover is done in Python, against the same
database, with the IDA Domain API
.RB ( ida_domain ;
see
.UR https://ida\-domain.docs.hex\-rays.com/
.UE ).
.TP 4
.B icli exec
runs Python in the database's process with
.B db
(an ida\-domain
.BR Database )
and
.B ida_domain
pre\-bound.
Its return value becomes ordinary records, so the result flows back into
.BR jq ,
templates and
.BR "icli apply" .
.TP
.B icli ref
searches the ida\-domain API reference shipped with the installed IDA, by
task or by name, and returns signatures with examples.
.TP
.B \-\-show\-code
on any command prints the ida\-domain code the command is equivalent to,
so a command that almost does what you want can be copied and adapted.
.PP
Under
.BR "icli serve" ,
.B exec
sessions keep their imports and variables between calls, and the same database can be served to
.BR ida\-mcp (1)
clients at the same time (see
.BR "icli serve \-\-mcp" ).
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Global options precede the command name.
Most can also be set in a configuration file or the environment (see
.BR CONFIGURATION ).
.TP
.BI \-\-db " path"
Use or create the database at
.IR path ,
bypassing the cache.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Analyse into a temporary database removed on exit.
.TP
.B \-\-read\-only
Open read\-only; any edit fails with status 13 (idat
.BR \-v ).
.TP
.BR \-\-analysis " auto|none|wait"
.B auto
(default) advances the database to the state the command needs.
.B none
never analyses; commands needing more fail with status 12.
.B wait
is
.B auto
but waits for another process that holds the database and is analysing,
instead of failing with status 11.
.TP
.BI \-\-analysis\-timeout " duration"
Stop advancing analysis after
.I duration
.RB ( 90s ", " 15m ", " 2h ).
The database is saved in state
.B analyzing
and the command runs on the partial result, exiting 3.
.TP
.BI \-f , " " \-\-format " fmt"
Stream output format:
.BR text ", " json ", " jsonl ", " csv ", " tsv ", " raw .
Default
.B text
on a terminal,
.B jsonl
otherwise.
See
.BR "OUTPUT FORMATS" .
.TP
.BI \-t , " " \-\-template " tmpl"
Render each record through a text template instead of
.BR \-\-format .
See
.BR "FIELDS AND TEMPLATES" .
.TP
.BI \-\-fields " list"
Fields to emit, in order
.RB ( \-\-fields=ea,name,size ).
.B icli schema
lists the valid fields per command.
.TP
.BI \-\-schema\-version " N"
Emit records using major schema version
.I N
(default: newest).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-header
Omit header rows in
.BR csv / tsv / text .
.TP
.BR \-0 ", " \-\-null
Terminate records with NUL (for
.BR "xargs \-0" ).
.TP
.BI \-\-addr " style"
How addresses print:
.B hex
(default,
.BR 0x401000 ),
.BR bare ,
.B seg
.RB ( .text:00401000 ),
.B rva
(from image base), or
.B file
(input file offset; empty if not file\-backed).
.TP
.BR \-\-color " auto|always|never"
Colorise text output, using IDA's color tags for listings and pseudocode.
Honours
.BR NO_COLOR .
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
No progress or informational messages.
Errors still print.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
More messages; repeat for kernel output
.RB ( \-vv
shows the IDA output window,
.B \-vvv
adds loader and plugin debug output, like idat
.BR \-z ).
.TP
.BI \-\-log " file"
Append all kernel messages to
.I file
(idat
.BR \-L ;
default
.BR $IDALOG ).
.TP
.BI \-\-set " KEY" = VALUE
Override a configuration directive for this invocation.
Unqualified keys target
.IR ida.cfg ;
a prefix selects another file:
.BR hexrays.MAX_FUNCSIZE=128 ,
.BR dwarf.DWARF_LOAD_LOCALS=NO ,
.BR lumina.LUMINA_TLS=YES .
Flag words accept named bits:
.BR ANALYSIS=+FLIRT,\-UNK ,
.BR hexrays.HEXOPTIONS=\-COLLAPSE_LVARS .
Unknown keys are an error (status 2), because a mistyped override is the
commonest cause of \(lqit did nothing\(rq.
Replaces idat
.B \-d
and
.BR \-D ;
.B icli
picks the right timing itself.
.TP
.BI \-\-plugin\-opt " name" : option
Pass an option to a plugin (idat
.BR \-O ).
.TP
.BI \-j , " " \-\-jobs " n"
Worker threads for parallel work
.RB ( "decompile \-\-all" ,
.BR "export c" ,
.BR diff ,
.BR "sig make" ,
.BR "lumina pull" ).
Default: number of CPUs.
Never changes results, only speed.
.TP
.BI \-C " dir"
Change to
.I dir
first, like
.BR "git \-C" .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-server
Do not forward to a running
.BR "icli serve" .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-plugins
Load only plugins the command strictly requires.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
For edits: print the journal records that would be written and change
nothing.
Exit 0 if there would be changes, 1 if the edit is a no\-op.
.TP
.B \-\-strict
Promote warnings to errors: a selector matching nothing, an ambiguous
demangled name, a truncated type, pseudocode containing
.B JUMPOUT
or
.BR __asm .
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-execute
Permit commands that run the target program
.RB ( debug ", " trace ).
Without it they exit 2.
.TP
.B \-\-show\-code
Do not run the command; print the ida\-domain Python it is equivalent to,
ready for
.BR "icli exec" .
Selectors and predicates are expanded into explicit loops and filters.
Exit 0.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the
.B icli
version, kernel version and build, edition (Pro, Home, Free, Classroom),
available decompilers, and exit.
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH LOAD OPTIONS
Accepted by every command whose target is an input file.
They are part of the cache key.
On an existing database they are an error (status 2) unless they match how
it was loaded.
.TP
.BI \-\-loader " name"
Force a loader by module name:
.BR pe ", " elf ", " macho ", " coff ", " dex ", " dsc
(dyld shared cache),
.BR uefi_fv ", " wasm ", " windmp ", " omf ", " ne ", " lx ", " xbe ,
.BR hexagon_mbn ", " ihex ", " ar ,
or
.B binary
for a flat file.
.B "icli loaders"
.I file
shows which loaders accept a file, in the order the GUI would offer them.
.TP
.BI \-\-processor " name\fR[\fP:variant\fR]\fP"
Force a processor module:
.BR metapc ", " arm ", " arm:ARMv7\-M ", " mips ", " mipsl ", " ppc ", " ppcl ,
.BR riscv ", " arc ", " tricore ", " hexagon ", " xtensa ", " v850 ", " m68k ,
.BR 8051 ", " dalvik ", " java ", " cli ", " wasm ", \&..."
.B "icli processors"
lists them.
.TP
.BR \-\-bitness " 16|32|64" ", " \-\-endian " little|big"
Defaults for raw images and bi\-endian processors.
.TP
.BI \-\-base " addr"
Load address in bytes (idat
.B \-b
used paragraphs).
.TP
.BI \-\-entry " addr"
Entry point for flat binaries.
.TP
.BI \-\-compiler " id\fR[\fP:abi\fR]\fP"
Compiler and ABI:
.BR gcc ", " clang ", " visual ", " borland ", " watcom ;
e.g.
.BR gcc:lp64 .
.TP
.BI \-\-segment " name" = start\-end\fR[\fP:class\fR][\fP:perm\fR][\fP@file\fR[\fP:offset\fR]]\fP
Create a segment, optionally backed by
.I file
(repeatable).
Describes bootrom + flash + SRAM + MMIO layouts in one command.
.TP
.BI \-\-svd " file.svd"
Import a CMSIS\-SVD peripheral description.
.TP
.BI \-\-load\-opt " loader" . key = value
Loader\-specific options:
.BR pe.resources=yes
(idat
.BR \-R ),
.BR macho.all_slices=yes ,
.BR elf.debug_dir=/usr/lib/debug ,
.BR dsc.modules=libsystem_c.dylib,libobjc.A.dylib .
.TP
.BI \-\-symbols " src\fR[\fP,src...\fR]\fP"
Debug information sources:
.BR auto
(default),
.BR none ,
.IR file.pdb ,
.IR file.debug ,
.IR Foo.dSYM ,
.B symsrv
(Microsoft symbol server via
.BR _NT_SYMBOL_PATH ),
.B debuginfod
(by build\-id via
.BR DEBUGINFOD_URLS ).
.TP
.BI \-\-encoding " name"
Default string encoding
.RB ( utf\-8 ", " cp1252 ", " utf\-16le ", \&...)."
.TP
.B \-\-no\-segmentation
Do not create segmentation (idat
.BR \-x ).
.TP
.BI \-\-pack " compress|pack|none"
How the database is saved (idat
.BR \-P+ ", " \-P ", " \-P\- ).
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH COMMANDS
Every command accepts
.BR \-h / \-\-help .
Below,
.I target
is as in
.B Targets
and
.I sel
is a selector.
Commands that accept selectors accept
.B \-
for standard input.
.\" ----------------------------------------------------------- triage
.SS Triage
.TP
.B icli identify \fR[\fB\-\-hash \fIalgo\fR,...] [\fB\-\-deep\fR] \fIfile\fR...
Describe files
.B without creating a database:
only the loaders'
.B accept_file
probes, compiler and packer heuristics, and hashing run.
One record per file:
.BR path ", " loader ", " loaders " (all accepting), " format ", " arch ,
.BR bitness ", " endian ", " compiler ", " packer ", " size ", " entropy ,
.BR sections " (with per\-section entropy), " md5 ", " sha1 ", " sha256 ,
.BR imphash ", " tlsh ", " ssdeep ", " pdb " (path and GUID), " build_id ,
.BR signed ", " signer ", " n_imports ", " n_exports .
.B \-\-deep
also runs the loader in a scratch database to count functions and strings.
Exits 1 if any file was accepted by no loader.
Takes thousands of files per minute; this is the corpus\-triage entry point.
.TP
.B icli info \fItarget\fR
Summarise a database: input name, size, hashes, loader, processor,
bitness, endianness, compiler/ABI, image base, entry points, counts
(segments; functions total/library/named/thunk; strings; types), applied
signatures and type libraries, debug info found, lifecycle state, creating
and last\-saving IDA version, cache key.
.TP
.B icli loaders \fR[\fIfile\fR]
List loaders; with a file, those accepting it with the formats and
processors they propose, in priority order.
.TP
.B icli processors \fR[\fIglob\fR]
List processor modules, variants, and which have a decompiler and an
assembler.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------- analysis
.SS Analysis
.TP
.B icli analyze \fR[\fIoptions\fR] \fItarget\fR [\fIsel\fR...]
Bring the database to
.BR analyzed .
With selectors, (re)queue only those ranges.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-reanalyze
Discard analysis results and run auto\-analysis again, keeping user edits
(re\-applied from the journal).
.TP
.BI \-\-with " pass\fR[\fP,pass...\fR]\fP"
Optional passes; moves to
.BR enriched :
.B lumina
(pull and apply metadata),
.BR pdb ", " dwarf ,
.BR rtti " (C++ class hierarchies), " eh " (exception tables),"
.BR golang ", " rust ", " swift ", " objc ,
.B findmain
(locate and name the real
.BR main ),
.B decompile
(decompile everything once to propagate types).
.TP
.BI \-\-without " pass\fR[\fP,pass...\fR]\fP"
Disable a default pass
.RB ( \-\-without=flirt ).
.TP
.BI \-\-sig " name" " \fR,\fP " \-\-til " name"
Extra FLIRT signature / type library to apply during analysis (repeatable).
.TP
.B \-\-progress
Progress as JSON lines on standard error:
.RS
.EX
{"_t":"progress","queue":"code","ea":"0x4012a0","pct":42}
.EE
.RE
.RE
.TP
.B icli status \fItarget\fR
Lifecycle state, pending items per analysis queue, lock holder (pid, host
or server socket), journal length, dirtiness relative to a vault revision.
Exits 0 if
.B analyzed
or later, 3 otherwise.
.\" ------------------------------------------------------------ query
.SS Query
.TP
.B icli list \fIkind\fR [\fIoptions\fR] \fItarget\fR [\fIsel\fR...]
List objects of
.IR kind ,
restricted to the selectors if given.
.I kind
is one of:
.BR functions ", " names ", " strings ", " imports ", " exports ", " entries ,
.BR segments ", " xrefs ", " types ", " tils ", " sigs ", " comments ,
.BR bookmarks ", " tags ", " problems ", " fixups ", " blocks ", " patches ,
.BR lvars " (decompiler local variables), " switches .
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-where " expr"
Filter with a predicate over the kind's fields:
.BR "\(aqsize > 0x400 && !lib\(aq" ,
.BR "\(aqmodule ~ \(dq(?i)ws2_32\(dq\(aq" .
Same language as selector predicates.
.TP
.BI \-\-match " glob" ", " \-\-regex " re"
Filter by name.
.TP
.BI \-\-sort " field\fR[\fP:desc\fR]\fP"
Order (default: by address).
.TP
.BI \-n , " " \-\-limit " N"
At most
.I N
records.
.TP
.B \-\-count
Print only the count.
.TP
.BR \-\-demangle " | " \-\-no\-demangle
Name style (default: as configured).
.RE
.TP
.B icli show \fItarget sel\fR...
Everything known about each address: segment, flags, item kind and size,
name, owning function, comments, operand representations, xrefs both ways,
type; for functions also prototype, frame layout and chunks.
.TP
.B icli disasm \fR[\fIoptions\fR] \fItarget sel\fR...
Disassembly.
A selector naming a function prints the whole function, chunks included.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-\-bytes " [\fIN\fP]"
Show opcode bytes.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-xrefs ", " \-\-no\-comments ", " \-\-no\-prefix
Trim the listing.
.TP
.BI \-\-syntax " name"
Assembler dialect offered by the module
.RB ( masm ", " gas ", " intel ", " att ).
.TP
.BR \-\-graph " [dot|gdl|json]"
Basic\-block graph instead of a listing.
.TP
.BR \-\-microcode "[=\fImaturity\fP]"
Hex\-Rays microcode at
.BR generated ", " preoptimized ", " locopt ", " calls ,
.BR glbopt1 ", " glbopt2 ", " glbopt3 ", or " lvars .
.RE
.IP
In
.B json
each record is one instruction:
.BR ea ", " size ", " bytes ", " mnem ", " operands
(text, type, value),
.BR text .
.TP
.B icli decompile \fR[\fIoptions\fR] \fItarget\fR [\fIsel\fR...]
Decompile the functions containing the selected addresses with the
decompiler matching the processor.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-all
Every non\-library function, in parallel with
.BR \-j .
.TP
.B \-\-with\-types
Prefix the output with the declarations of every user type referenced,
giving a self\-contained C file.
.TP
.B \-\-at\-line
For each selected address print only the pseudocode line(s) it maps to,
prefixed by the function name.
Ideal for call sites piped from
.BR xrefs .
.TP
.B \-\-ctree
Emit the ctree as JSON (node, ea, type, children).
.TP
.B \-\-line\-map
In
.B json
output, map each line to the addresses it covers and each local variable
to its storage.
.TP
.B \-\-fresh
Ignore pseudocode cached in the database.
.TP
.BI \-\-hexrays\-option " \fR[+|\-]\fPNAME\fR,...\fP"
Toggle
.B HEXOPTIONS
bits for this run.
.RE
.IP
Failures do not abort
.BR \-\-all :
each failed function yields a record with
.BR status=failed ,
.B hexrays_err
and the failing address; exit status is 3.
A single requested function that fails exits 8.
.TP
.B icli xrefs \fR[\fB\-\-to\fR|\fB\-\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-type \fIt\fR] [\fB\-\-depth \fIN\fR] \fItarget sel\fR...
Cross\-references to (default) or from the selection; types
.BR call ", " jump ", " flow ", " read ", " write ", " offset ", " text ", " info .
Records:
.BR from ", " to ", " type ", " func_from ", " func_to ", " user .
.TP
.B icli callgraph \fR[\fB\-\-callers\fR|\fB\-\-callees\fR] [\fB\-\-depth \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-graph \fIdot\fR|\fIgdl\fR|\fIjson\fR] \fItarget sel\fR...
Call graph rooted at the selected functions.
.TP
.B icli search \fR[\fIoptions\fR] \fItarget\fR [\fIsel\fR...]
Search the selected ranges (default: everything).
Exactly one of:
.BI \-\-bytes " \(dq55 8B EC ?? ?? 83\(dq"
(IDA binary pattern),
.BI \-\-imm " value" ,
.BI \-\-insn " \(dqcall *ds:*Alloc*\(dq"
(instruction pattern),
.BI \-\-text " re"
(over listing lines),
.BI \-\-pseudo " re"
(over pseudocode; decompiles as needed),
.BI \-\-string " re"
(over string literals, reporting referencing functions),
.BI \-\-crypto
(known constants: AES S\-boxes, SHA/MD5 IVs, CRC tables, ...).
.TP
.B icli resolve \fR[\fB\-\-ranges\fR] \fItarget sel\fR...
Evaluate selectors and print the resulting addresses.
The canonical way to test a selector and to turn names into addresses for
other tools.
Exits 1 if the result is empty.
.\" ------------------------------------------------------------- edit
.SS Edit
All edit commands are idempotent, accept
.B \-\-dry\-run
and
.BI \-\-message " text"
(journal annotation), print one record per change (or
.BR unchanged ),
and expand
.B {field}
templates per selected item.
A value previously set by a user (as opposed to auto\-analysis) is only
overwritten with
.BR \-\-force ;
otherwise the conflict exits 9.
.TP
.B icli rename \fR[\fIoptions\fR] \fItarget sel name\fR
.TQ
.B icli rename \fR[\fIoptions\fR] \fItarget\fR \fB\-\fR|\fImap.tsv\fR
Set names.
From a file or standard input, each line is
.IB sel \et name
or a JSON object with
.B ea
and
.BR name .
.I name
is a template:
.B \(aqf_{hash:.8}\(aq
names each function after its body hash, stable across builds.
Options:
.BR \-\-local ", " \-\-public ", " \-\-weak ,
.BI \-\-regex " s/re/repl/"
(rewrite existing names),
.BI \-\-lvar " func"
(rename a decompiler local variable),
.B \-\-unique
(suffix
.BR _1 ", " _2
on collision instead of failing),
.B \-\-clear
(restore the dummy name).
.TP
.B icli comment \fR[\fB\-\-kind \fIk\fR] [\fB\-\-append\fR] \fItarget sel text\fR
Set a comment;
.I k
is
.BR regular ", " repeatable ", " anterior ", " posterior ", " function ,
or
.B pseudocode
(attached to the ctree item at that address).
Empty
.I text
removes it.
.TP
.B icli type \fIsubcommand\fR ...
.RS
.TP
.B type set \fItarget sel decl\fR
Apply a C declaration to an address, function or local variable.
.I decl
is a template:
.BR "\(aqNTSTATUS __stdcall {name}(PDEVICE_OBJECT, PIRP)\(aq" .
.B \-\-propagate
re\-decompiles callers so the new type flows outward.
.TP
.B type get \fItarget sel\fR
Print the type at an address.
.TP
.B type add \fItarget\fR \fIfile.h\fR|\fB\-\fR
Parse declarations into local types using the clang\-based parser
.RB ( \-\-parser=legacy
for the old one).
.BR \-I ", " \-D " and " \-\-target " \fItriple\fP"
are passed to the preprocessor.
Identical types are left alone; a conflicting definition exits 9 unless
.BR \-\-replace .
.TP
.B type import \fItarget source name\fR...
Copy types from a type library or another database.
.TP
.B type del \fItarget name\fR...
Delete local types.
.TP
.B type dump \fItarget\fR [\fIname\fR...]
Print local types as a compilable, topologically sorted C header.
.TP
.B type op \fItarget sel\fR \fB\-\-operand \fIN\fR \fB\-\-as \fIkind\fR[\fB:\fIarg\fR]
Operand representation:
.BR hex ", " dec ", " char ", " offset[:base] ", " enum:name ,
.BR stroff:struct ", " stkvar .
.TP
.B type callsite \fItarget sel decl\fR
Override the prototype at one call site.
.RE
.TP
.B icli func \fBcreate\fR|\fBdelete\fR|\fBset\fR|\fBtail\fR ...
Create a function
.RB ( \-\-end
optional), delete it (keeping instructions), change bounds, flags
.RB ( \-\-flags +noret,\-lib )
or frame, add/remove chunks.
.TP
.B icli make \fIkind target sel\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
Convert items:
.B code
(and analyse onward),
.BR byte ", " word ", " dword ", " qword ", " float ", " double ,
.B string
.RB [ \-\-encoding ],
.B array \-\-count
.IR n ,
.BI "struct \-\-type " name ,
.B offset
.RB [ \-\-base ],
.BR align ,
.B unknown
(undefine);
.B \-\-jumptable
.I spec
declares a switch table.
.TP
.B icli patch \fIsubcommand\fR ...
.RS
.TP
.B patch bytes \fItarget sel hex\fR
Patch bytes in the database.
.TP
.B patch asm \fItarget sel insn\fR...
Assemble and patch (processors with an assembler).
.TP
.B patch nop \fItarget sel\fR
Replace items with same\-length NOPs.
.TP
.B patch revert \fItarget\fR [\fIsel\fR...]
Restore original bytes.
.RE
.IP
Writing the patched file is an export:
.BR "icli export exe" ,
.BR "icli export dif" .
.TP
.B icli tag \fR[\fB\-\-remove\fR] [\fB\-\-color \fIrrggbb\fR] \fItarget sel tag\fR...
Attach free\-form tags (and optionally a background colour) to items.
Tags are selectable
.RB ( tag:crypto )
and survive in the database.
Bookmarks are tags named
.BR bookmark:\fItext\fR .
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------- journal
.SS Journal
.TP
.B icli apply \fR[\fIoptions\fR] \fItarget\fR [\fIjournal.jsonl\fR|\fB\-\fR]
Replay journal records (any record an edit command emits, and any query
record that carries the same fields).
.BR \-\-on\-conflict=fail|skip|ours|theirs ;
.B \-\-only rename,type
(restrict kinds);
.B \-\-rebase
translates addresses when the target has a different base or is a
different build, using function matching (see
.BR diff ).
.TP
.B icli log \fR[\fB\-\-since \fIrev\fR|\fItime\fR] [\fB\-\-author \fIu\fR] [\fB\-\-kind \fIk\fR] \fItarget\fR [\fIsel\fR...]
Print the journal, oldest first: an audit log of who changed what.
.TP
.B icli undo \fR[\fB\-\-to \fIrev\fR|\fB\-n \fIN\fR] \fItarget\fR
Revert the last
.I N
entries (default 1) by applying their inverses, which are themselves
journaled.
.\" -------------------------------------------------------- knowledge
.SS Knowledge
.TP
.B icli sig \fIsubcommand\fR ...
FLIRT signatures.
.RS
.TP
.B sig apply \fItarget name\fR...|\fBauto\fR
Apply
.I .sig
files by name (searched in
.IR $IDAUSR/sig/ proc
then
.IR $IDADIR/sig/ proc )
or path;
.B auto
uses the loader's startup signatures.
Reports matches per file.
.TP
.B sig match \fItarget name\fR...
What a signature file would rename, without applying.
.TP
.B sig make \fR[\fIoptions\fR] \fB\-o \fIout.sig\fR \fIsource\fR...
Build signatures from databases or static libraries
.RI ( .a ", " .lib ;
loaded with the
.B ar
loader).
.BI \-\-library\-name " text" ,
.BI \-\-select " sel"
(which functions),
.B \-\-pat\-only
(stop at
.IR .pat ),
.BR \-\-collisions " fail|skip|first"
(replaces the interactive
.I .exc
editing step of
.BR sigmake (1)).
.TP
.B sig list \fR[\fB\-\-processor \fIp\fR]
Available signature files and their library names.
.RE
.TP
.B icli til \fIsubcommand\fR ...
Type libraries:
.B list
(available
.IR .til ),
.B dump
.I file.til
.RI [ name ...]
(as C),
.B make
.BI \-o " out.til"
.RB [ \-\-target
.IR triple ]
.RB [ \-I
.IR dir ]
.IR header ...
(replaces
.BR tilib (1)
for the common case),
.B merge
.BI \-o " out.til"
.IR in.til ...,
.B export
.I target
.BI \-o " out.til"
(local types as a library).
.TP
.B icli lumina \fIsubcommand\fR ...
Lumina, using the server from
.I ida.cfg
or
.BI \-\-server " host" : port .
.RS
.TP
.B lumina pull \fR[\fB\-\-apply\fR] \fItarget\fR [\fIsel\fR...]
Fetch metadata for the selected (default: all) functions.
Without
.BR \-\-apply ,
print candidates (name, prototype, comments, frame,
.BR score )
as records ready for review and
.BR "icli apply" .
.TP
.B lumina push \fItarget\fR [\fIsel\fR...]
Push metadata of selected user\-named functions; refuses dummy names.
.TP
.B lumina del\fR|\fBhistory \fItarget sel\fR...
Delete own metadata; show a function's history.
.RE
.TP
.B icli load \fIkind target file\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
Add data to an existing database:
.BR pdb ", " dwarf " (separate debug file or .dSYM), " svd ", " map
(linker map),
.BR idc ", " names " (address/name CSV or MAP), " coverage
(drcov, lighthouse; sets the
.B coverage
field),
.B binary
.BI \-\-at " addr"
(another blob as a segment),
.B snapshot
(memory dump).
.\" ----------------------------------------------------------- output
.SS Output
.TP
.B icli export \fIformat\fR [\fIoptions\fR] \fItarget\fR [\fIsel\fR...]
Produce a file from the database to
.B \-o
.I path
(standard output by default).
The format is named explicitly; it is never guessed from the extension.
Formats that take a selector honour it; the others write the whole
database.
.B \-o
accepts templates: with a per\-item template such as
.BR \-o\ \(aqsrc/{name}.c\(aq ,
one file is written per selected item.
See
.B Export formats
under
.BR "OUTPUT FORMATS" .
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------- compare
.SS Compare
.TP
.B icli diff \fR[\fIoptions\fR] \fIold new\fR
Compare two databases (or input files, analysed first) function by
function.
Records have
.B diff
=
.BR identical ", " changed ", " added ", " removed ", " renamed ,
plus
.BR similarity " (0.0\-1.0), " ea ", " other_ea ", and " changed_blocks .
Exit 0 if identical, 1 if differences were found (like
.BR diff (1)).
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-match " strategy\fR[\fP,strategy...\fR]\fP"
Matching rounds in order:
.BR name ", " hash
(operand\-agnostic body hash),
.BR flirt ", " lumina ", " structural
(CFG and call\-graph neighbourhood, constants, strings).
Default:
.BR name,hash,lumina,structural .
.TP
.BI \-\-threshold " score"
Minimum similarity for
.B changed
(default 0.6).
.TP
.BR \-\-pseudocode ", " \-\-asm
Attach a unified diff of pseudocode or normalised disassembly to each
changed function.
.TP
.BI \-\-emit\-journal " file"
Write journal records that port
.IR old 's
user names, types and comments onto
.IR new .
.RE
.TP
.B icli port \fR[\fB\-\-what \fInames\fR,\fItypes\fR,\fIcomments\fR,\fItags\fR] [\fB\-\-match \fI...\fR] \fIfrom to\fR
Shorthand for
.B diff \-\-emit\-journal
piped into
.BR "apply \-\-rebase" :
carry annotations from an analysed build onto a new one in one step.
Edits land in
.IR to 's
journal and can be reviewed with
.B log
or reverted with
.BR undo .
.\" ------------------------------------------------------- automation
.SS Automation
.TP
.B icli do \fR[\fB\-\-keep\-going\fR] \fItarget\fR \fB\-\-\fR \fIstep\fR [\fB::\fR \fIstep\fR]...
.TQ
.B icli do \fItarget\fR \fB@\fIrecipe\fR [\fIstep\fR...]
Open
.I target
once and run each
.I step
\(em any command line with the target omitted \(em left to right.
This is the ordered\-pipeline mode: one load, many operations, many outputs.
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Analysis runs only where a step needs it, so steps before the first
query can change how analysis proceeds (apply types, signatures, segments).
.IP \(bu
A step's selector may be
.BR % ,
meaning the records produced by the previous step.
.IP \(bu
The database is saved once, at the end, and only if every step succeeded
(or
.B \-\-keep\-going
was given).
.BR \-\-no\-save
discards all changes; useful for pure reports.
.IP \(bu
A recipe is a file in
.I $IDAUSR/icli/recipes/
.RI ( name .icli)
with one step per line;
.BI @ name
splices it in.
.RE
.TP
.B icli batch \fR[\fB\-\-keep\-going\fR] \fItarget\fR [\fIfile\fR|\fB\-\fR]
Like
.BR do ,
but steps are read one per line from a file or standard input; each step's
records are written as they complete, tagged with
.BR step .
For programs that drive
.B icli
interactively without IDAPython.
.TP
.B icli exec \fR[\fIoptions\fR] \fItarget\fR [\fB\-c \fIcode\fR | \fIfile.py\fR | \fB\-\fR] [\fB\-\-\fR \fIargs\fR...]
Run Python against the database, after bringing it to
.BR analyzed .
Semantics match the
.B execute_python
tool of
.BR ida\-mcp (1).
API documentation:
.UR https://ida\-domain.docs.hex\-rays.com/
.UE .
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.B db
is the current ida\-domain
.BR Database ;
.B ida_domain
and the classic
.B ida_*
modules are importable as usual.
.IP \(bu
If the code ends with an expression, its value is the result.
Otherwise, if it defines
.BR run(db) ,
.B main(db)
or
.BR execute(db) ,
that function is called and its return value is the result.
.IP \(bu
The result becomes records: a mapping is one record, an iterable of
mappings is a stream, and a scalar is
.BR {"_t":"value","value":...} .
Records that carry
.B ea
and journal fields
.RB ( name ", " type ", " comment ", \&...)"
can be piped straight into
.BR "icli apply" .
.IP \(bu
The code's own
.B stdout
and
.B stderr
are kept apart from the results: with
.B \-f json
they are returned as
.B stdout
and
.B stderr
fields, otherwise they are passed through to standard error.
.IP \(bu
Changes the code makes are journaled as one
.B exec
record holding the code's SHA\-256 (and the code itself unless
.BR \-\-no\-record\-code ),
so
.B icli undo
reverts a whole
.B exec
at once.
.RE
.IP
Options:
.RS
.TP
.BI \-c " code"
Code on the command line.
Otherwise a file, or
.B \-
for standard input.
.TP
.BI \-\-each " sel"
Run once per selected item with
.B item
(the record, with all its fields) and
.B ea
bound; results are concatenated.
.TP
.BI \-\-session " name"
Keep imports, variables and definitions between calls.
Requires
.BR "icli serve" ;
the session lives as long as the server's lease.
Without it every call starts with fresh globals.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " duration"
Abort the code after
.I duration
(default 6m; the initial analysis wait is not counted).
The database is rolled back to the state before the call.
.TP
.B \-\-read\-only
Fail with status 13 if the code tries to modify the database.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-save
Discard the code's changes after it returns.
.TP
.BR \-\-lang " py|idc"
IDC instead of Python (only a trailing expression is supported).
.RE
.IP
.B sys.argv
receives
.IR args ;
.B sys.exit(\fIn\fP)
and
.B qexit(\fIn\fP)
set the exit status.
An uncaught exception exits 16 with the traceback on standard error.
.TP
.B icli ref \fR[\fB\-n \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-full\fR] \fIquery\fR...
Search the ida\-domain API reference of the
.B installed
IDA (so it never disagrees with the API it describes), by task or by name:
.RS
.EX
icli ref "decompile function"
icli ref xrefs to address
icli ref Functions.get_callers
.EE
.RE
.IP
Each hit gives a signature, a one\-line description and a short example.
.B \-\-full
prints the whole entry;
.B \-f jsonl
returns records with
.BR symbol ", " signature ", " doc ", " example .
Works offline and without a target.
The index is the one served by the
.B reference
tool of
.BR ida\-mcp (1);
the full documentation is at
.UR https://ida\-domain.docs.hex\-rays.com/
.UE .
.TP
.B icli assert \fItarget sel cond\fR
Check a condition on the size of a selection and exit 1 if it fails;
.I cond
is
.RB ( == | != | < | <= | > | >= )
.IR n .
.B "icli assert app.exe \(aqfunc:*[hexrays_err != 0]\(aq \(aq<= 3\(aq"
fails a CI job when more than three functions stop decompiling.
Exit 0 prints nothing; exit 1 prints the offending items.
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------- dynamic
.SS Dynamic
These commands execute the target program and require
.BR \-\-allow\-execute .
Backends:
.BR linux ", " win32 ", " mac ", " gdb ", " windbg ", " bochs ", " dalvik ,
.BR pin ", " replay ;
remote with
.BI \-\-remote " host" : port
and
.B $ICLI_DEBUG_PASSWORD
(idat
.BR \-r ).
.TP
.B icli debug run \fR[\fB\-\-debugger \fId\fR] [\fB\-\-break \fIsel\fR[\fB:\fIcond\fR]...] [\fB\-\-regs \fIlist\fR] [\fB\-\-dump \fIexpr\fB:\fIsize\fR] [\fB\-\-timeout \fIt\fR] \fItarget\fR [\fB\-\-\fR \fIargs\fR...]
Start the program; at each breakpoint emit a record (thread, address,
registers, memory, stack trace) and continue.
Unanswerable debugger prompts take their defaults from
.IR exceptions.cfg .
Exit 10 on timeout.
.TP
.B icli debug attach \fR[\fB\-\-pid \fIN\fR|\fB\-\-name \fIproc\fR] \fItarget\fR [\fIas for run\fR]
Attach to a running process.
.TP
.B icli debug snapshot \fR[\fB\-\-at \fIsel\fR] \fItarget\fR
Run to an address (default: entry), copy process memory into the database,
and mark the database for reanalysis.
.TP
.B icli trace \fR[\fB\-\-mode \fIinsn\fR|\fIblock\fR|\fIfunc\fR] [\fB\-\-range \fIsel\fR] [\fB\-\-coverage\fR] \fItarget\fR [\fB\-\-\fR \fIargs\fR...]
Record an execution trace as records;
.B \-\-coverage
emits only executed basic blocks and fills the
.B coverage
field.
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------- storage
.SS Storage
.TP
.B icli db \fIsubcommand\fR ...
.RS
.TP
.B db path \fItarget\fR
Print the database path (computes the cache key; creates nothing).
.TP
.B db create \fItarget\fR \fB\-o \fIdb.i64\fR
Load and analyse into an explicit file.
.TP
.BR "db pack" " [" \-\-mode " compress|pack] \fIdb\fR, " "db unpack \fIdb\fR"
Convert between a single
.I .i64
and its components
.RI ( .id0 ", " .id1 ", " .id2 ", " .nam ", " .til ).
.TP
.B db upgrade \fR[\fB\-o \fIout.i64\fR] \fIold.idb\fR
Convert 32\-bit
.I .idb
and older formats to the current
.IR .i64 .
.TP
.B db check \fIdb\fR
Verify b\-tree integrity; exit 14 if corrupt.
.TP
.B db gc \fIdb\fR
Compact the b\-tree.
.TP
.B db tag \fIname target\fR
Register a handle usable as
.BI @ name .
.TP
.B db copy \fIsrc dst\fR
Copy safely while in use (takes a read lock).
.TP
.B db unlock \fR[\fB\-\-force\fR] \fIdb\fR
Remove a stale lock (verifies the holder is gone unless
.BR \-\-force ).
.RE
.TP
.B icli cache ls\fR|\fBrm \fItarget\fR|\fBkey \fItarget\fR|\fBprune \fR[\fB\-\-older\-than \fId\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-size \fIs\fR] [\fB\-\-orphans\fR]
Inspect and maintain the database cache.
.TP
.B icli vault \fIsubcommand\fR ...
IDA Teams, mirroring
.BR hv (1):
.BR sync ", " checkout ", " add ", " commit ", " revert ", " diff ", " log ", " info .
.B vault merge
performs the three\-way database merge non\-interactively; conflicts are
records, resolved by
.BR \-\-strategy=ours|theirs|fail .
.B vault commit
refuses a database in state
.B analyzing
unless
.BR \-\-force .
.TP
.B icli serve \fR[\fIoptions\fR] \fItarget\fR...
Keep databases open in a background process listening on a Unix socket
(named pipe on Windows) at
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/icli/ key .sock .
Every
.B icli
command on a served database is forwarded transparently: no load, no
b\-tree warm\-up, millisecond answers.
.BR \-\-detach ,
.BI \-\-idle\-timeout " d"
(default 30m),
.BI \-\-save\-every " d" ,
.BI \-\-listen " addr"
(TCP, requires
.BR \-\-token\-file ),
.BR \-\-stop .
.IP
The server is an ida\-nexus database service: it owns the workers,
leases and cancellation, and attaches to a database already open in the IDA
GUI instead of opening a second copy.
.B \-\-mcp
.RI [ stdio | http:\fIaddr\fP ]
also exposes the same session as an MCP server with the
.BR ida\-mcp (1)
tool set; edits from MCP clients land in the same journal.
.\" ------------------------------------------------------------- meta
.SS Meta
.TP
.B icli config get\fR|\fBset\fR|\fBunset\fR|\fBlist \fR[\fB\-\-global\fR|\fB\-\-project\fR] [\fIkey\fR [\fIvalue\fR]]
Read and write
.B icli
configuration
.RI ( ida.cfg
is never written; use
.BR \-\-set ).
.TP
.B icli schema \fR[\fIcommand\fR [\fIkind\fR]]
JSON Schema of the records a command emits
.RB ( icli.function/1 ", " icli.xref/1 ", \&...)."
.TP
.B icli completion bash\fR|\fBzsh\fR|\fBfish\fR|\fBpowershell
Shell completion; names and selectors complete against the database of the
target already on the command line.
.TP
.B icli help \fR[\fIcommand\fR|\fItopic\fR]
Topics:
.BR selectors ", " fields ", " templates ", " formats ", " exit\-codes ,
.BR journal ", " cache ", " recipes ", " settings ", " exec .
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH SELECTORS
A selector denotes a set of items.
It is evaluated against the database after it reaches the state the
command needs, and is a
.I snapshot:
inside
.BR "icli do" ,
a later step re\-evaluates its own selectors against the then\-current
database.
.SS Address atoms
.TS
l lx.
\f(CB0x401000\fP, \f(CB401000h\fP, \f(CB0x8000_1234\fP	T{
linear address (\f(CB_\fP ignored)
T}
\f(CB0d4198400\fP	T{
decimal; a bare decimal is rejected as ambiguous
T}
\f(CBmain\fP, \f(CB?OnPaint@CView@@MAEXPAVCDC@@@Z\fP	T{
name, mangled or demangled
T}
\f(CB"CView::OnPaint"\fP	T{
demangled name (all overloads)
T}
\f(CB.text:401000\fP, \f(CBseg000:0100\fP	T{
segment\-relative
T}
\f(CBrva:0x1000\fP, \f(CBoff:0x400\fP	T{
image\-base relative; input file offset
T}
\f(CBmain+0x2c\fP, \f(CB$entry\-4\fP	T{
arithmetic on any atom
T}
\f(CB$entry $base $min $max\fP	T{
entry point, image base, bounds
T}
.TE
.SS Ranges
.TS
l lx.
\f(CB0x1000..0x2000\fP	T{
half\-open [start, end)
T}
\f(CB0x1000+0x100\fP	T{
start and size
T}
\f(CBmain..\fP	T{
to the end of the segment
T}
.TE
.SS Typed selectors
.TS
l lx.
\f(CBfunc:\fIglob\fP	T{
functions by name (\f(CBfunc:*\fP all)
T}
\f(CBfunc@\fIaddr\fP	T{
the function containing \fIaddr\fP (all chunks)
T}
\f(CBseg:\fIname\fP	T{
a segment (\f(CBseg:.text\fP, \f(CBseg:__TEXT.__text\fP)
T}
\f(CBname:\fIglob\fP	T{
any named item
T}
\f(CBstr:\fIglob\fP	T{
string literals by value
T}
\f(CBimp:\fImod\fP!\fIsym\fP	T{
imports (\f(CBimp:*!recv\fP, \f(CBimp:kernel32!Create*\fP)
T}
\f(CBexp:\fIglob\fP	T{
exports
T}
\f(CBentry\fP	T{
entry points, TLS callbacks, init arrays
T}
\f(CBtype:\fIglob\fP	T{
local types; data items of that type
T}
\f(CBbytes:\fIhex\fP	T{
addresses where a byte pattern occurs
T}
\f(CBtag:\fIt\fP	T{
items tagged with \fBicli tag\fP
T}
\f(CBlib thunk noret dummy named\fP	T{
function classes
T}
\f(CBpatched lumina problem\fP	T{
patched bytes; Lumina\-enriched; problem list
T}
\f(CBdiff:\fIclass\fP	T{
diff records (\f(CBchanged\fP, \f(CBadded\fP, ...)
T}
\f(CB@\fIfile\fP	T{
selectors listed in a file, one per line
T}
\f(CB%\fP	T{
the previous step's records (\fBicli do\fP only)
T}
\f(CB\-\fP	T{
standard input
T}
.TE
.PP
Globs are the default;
.BI / re /\fR[\fPi\fR]\fP
gives a regular expression:
.BR func:/^ssl_/i .
.SS Graph operators
.TS
l lx.
\f(CBcallers(\fIs\fP)\fP, \f(CBcallees(\fIs\fP)\fP	T{
direct callers / callees of functions in \fIs\fP
T}
\f(CBcallers(\fIs\fP,\fIN\fP)\fP, \f(CBcallers*(\fIs\fP)\fP	T{
up to depth \fIN\fP; transitive closure
T}
\f(CBxrefs(\fIs\fP)\fP, \f(CBdrefs(\fIs\fP)\fP, \f(CBcrefs(\fIs\fP)\fP	T{
items referencing \fIs\fP (all, data, code)
T}
\f(CBrefs(\fIs\fP)\fP	T{
items referenced by \fIs\fP
T}
\f(CBblocks(\fIs\fP)\fP	T{
basic blocks of the functions in \fIs\fP
T}
\f(CBfunc(\fIs\fP)\fP	T{
the functions containing \fIs\fP
T}
\f(CBuses_type(\fIt\fP)\fP	T{
functions whose prototype or lvars use type \fIt\fP
T}
.TE
.SS Set operators
.TS
l lx.
\f(CBa , b\fP  or  \f(CBa | b\fP	T{
union
T}
\f(CBa & b\fP	T{
intersection
T}
\f(CBa ~ b\fP	T{
difference
T}
\f(CB!a\fP	T{
complement (within the kind of \fIa\fP)
T}
\f(CB( ... )\fP	T{
grouping
T}
.TE
.PP
Difference is
.BR ~ ,
not
.BR \- ,
so it never collides with address arithmetic.
.SS Predicates
Any selector may be followed by one or more
.BI [ expr ]
filters over its items'
.BR FIELDS :
.PP
.EX
func:*[size > 0x400][xrefs_to >= 10]       big and popular
func:sub_*[insns > 200 && hexrays_err != 0]
                                           large, unnamed, undecompilable
str:*http*[xrefs_to == 0]                  unreferenced URLs
callers(imp:*!VirtualProtect, 3)[!lib]     user code near VirtualProtect
diff:changed[similarity < 0.9]             substantially changed
.EE
.PP
Operators:
.B == != < <= > >= && || !
and
.B ~
(regex match on strings,
.BR "module ~ \(dq(?i)ws2\(dq" ).
Fields that need the decompiler
.RB ( pseudocode ", " hexrays_err ", " lvars )
trigger decompilation; this is correct but can be slow.
.SS Quoting
Selectors containing
.BR "( ) | & ! * [ ] ~ $"
must be quoted for the shell.
Single quotes are recommended.
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH FIELDS AND TEMPLATES
.SS Common fields
.B "icli schema"
is authoritative; the most used fields are:
.PP
.TS
l lx.
\fBea\fP, \fBend\fP, \fBsize\fP	T{
start, end, size in bytes
T}
\fBkind\fP	T{
function, data, string, type, import, xref, diff, ...
T}
\fBname\fP, \fBdemangled\fP, \fBmangled\fP	T{
names
T}
\fBtype\fP	T{
C declaration or prototype
T}
\fBsegment\fP, \fBflags\fP	T{
segment name; LIB, THUNK, NORET, ...
T}
\fBlib\fP, \fBthunk\fP, \fBnoret\fP, \fBdummy\fP	T{
booleans
T}
\fBxrefs_to\fP, \fBxrefs_from\fP	T{
reference counts
T}
\fBcallers\fP, \fBcallees\fP	T{
distinct calling / called functions
T}
\fBblocks\fP, \fBinsns\fP, \fBcyclomatic\fP	T{
CFG metrics
T}
\fBhash\fP	T{
operand\-agnostic body hash (stable across rebuilds)
T}
\fBbytes\fP, \fBbytes_sha256\fP	T{
raw bytes (hex, truncated), their hash
T}
\fBcomment\fP, \fBrcomment\fP	T{
regular, repeatable comment
T}
\fBflirt\fP, \fBlumina\fP	T{
matching library; none|pulled|conflict
T}
\fBcoverage\fP	T{
hit count from \fBload coverage\fP / \fBtrace\fP
T}
\fBtags\fP	T{
tags from \fBicli tag\fP
T}
\fBvalue\fP, \fBencoding\fP	T{
string literal contents, encoding
T}
\fBmodule\fP, \fBordinal\fP	T{
imports and exports
T}
\fBdisasm\fP	T{
disassembly text
T}
\fBpseudocode\fP, \fBhexrays_err\fP	T{
decompiler output; error code (0 = ok)
T}
\fBmicrocode\fP	T{
microcode at \fB\-\-maturity\fP
T}
\fBdiff\fP, \fBsimilarity\fP, \fBother_ea\fP	T{
diff class, score, matched address
T}
\fBindex\fP, \fBcount\fP	T{
position in, and size of, the result set
T}
\fBinput\fP, \fBdb\fP, \fBprocessor\fP	T{
context
T}
.TE
.SS Templates
.B \-t
.I tmpl
renders each record as text.
Placeholders are
.BI { field }
with an optional Python\-style format spec
.BI { field : spec }\fR:\fP
.PP
.TS
l lx.
\f(CB{ea}\fP	T{
0x401000 (per \fB\-\-addr\fP)
T}
\f(CB{size:>8}\fP	T{
right\-aligned in 8 columns
T}
\f(CB{size:#x}\fP	T{
hexadecimal with prefix
T}
\f(CB{name:<40.40}\fP	T{
padded and truncated to 40
T}
\f(CB{hash:.8}\fP	T{
first 8 characters
T}
\f(CB{tags:,}\fP	T{
list joined by commas
T}
\f(CB{{\fP  \f(CB}}\fP	T{
literal braces
T}
.TE
.PP
Escapes
.BR \en ", " \et ", " \e0
are recognised.
A record gets a trailing newline unless the template ends with
.BR \ec .
.B \-\-header
.I tmpl
and
.B \-\-footer
.I tmpl
are rendered once, before and after the records, with
.B count
available.
.PP
Templates also appear in edit arguments
.RB ( rename ,
.BR "type set" ,
.BR comment )
and in
.B \-o
paths, where a per\-item template writes one file per item.
Characters invalid in file names are replaced with
.BR _ .
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH OUTPUT FORMATS
.SS Stream formats
Records written to standard output by query, edit and compare commands.
.TP 8
.B text
Aligned columns, optionally coloured.
For people; not a stable interface.
.TP
.B jsonl
One JSON object per record.
Default when standard output is not a terminal.
Every record carries
.B _t
(record type) so mixed streams demultiplex with
.BR jq .
Addresses are strings, so 64\-bit values survive tools that use doubles.
.TP
.B json
One document:
.RS
.EX
{"schema":"icli.function/1", "database":{...},
 "records":[...], "warnings":[...]}
.EE
.RE
.TP
.BR csv ", " tsv
RFC 4180 with a header row; nested values are JSON in one cell.
.TP
.B raw
The natural payload: pseudocode for
.BR decompile ,
listing text for
.BR disasm ,
bytes for
.BR "export bin" .
.PP
Diagnostics never go to standard output.
With
.B json
or
.BR jsonl ,
diagnostics on standard error are JSON lines too:
.RS
.EX
{"_t":"diag","level":"warning","code":"NOMATCH","msg":"..."}
.EE
.RE
.SS Export formats
Named explicitly to
.BR "icli export" .
.PP
.TS
l l lx.
\fBformat\fP	\fBselection\fP	T{
\fBcontents\fP
T}
i64	yes	T{
database; with a selector, a minimal database holding only the
T}
		T{
selected functions, their callees' prototypes and the types they
T}
		T{
use \(em a self\-contained decompiler bug reproducer
T}
asm	yes	T{
assemblable source (OFILE_ASM); \fB\-\-with\-types\fP
T}
lst	yes	T{
listing with addresses (OFILE_LST)
T}
html	yes	T{
hyperlinked listing (GENFLG_GENHTML); \fB\-\-highlight\fP \fIrecords\fP
T}
map	no	T{
MAP file (OFILE_MAP); \fB\-\-segments \-\-demangle \-\-locals\fP
T}
idc	no	T{
IDC script recreating all user annotations (OFILE_IDC)
T}
python	no	T{
the same as IDAPython
T}
journal	no	T{
the edit journal (= \fBicli log \-f jsonl\fP)
T}
dif	no	T{
patch list (OFILE_DIF)
T}
exe	no	T{
patched input file (OFILE_EXE); \fB\-\-in\-place\fP needs \fB\-\-force\fP
T}
bin	yes	T{
raw bytes of the selected ranges
T}
c	yes	T{
pseudocode, preceded by needed declarations; \fB\-j\fP parallel
T}
cpp	yes	T{
same, with C++ class reconstruction
T}
mc	yes	T{
microcode at \fB\-\-maturity\fP
T}
h	no	T{
local types as a C header (= \fBtype dump\fP)
T}
til	no	T{
local types as a type library
T}
sig, pat	yes	T{
FLIRT signature / pattern of the selected functions
T}
dot, gdl	yes	T{
call graph (\fB\-\-graph calls|flow|xrefs\fP)
T}
svg	yes	T{
rendered graph
T}
sqlite	no	T{
every \fBlist\fP kind as a table, for ad\-hoc SQL
T}
sarif	yes	T{
SARIF 2.1 results, one per selected item, for code scanning
T}
.TE
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B icli
reads its own settings from TOML and kernel settings from the usual
.I .cfg
files.
Precedence, highest first:
.IP 1. 4
command\-line options;
.IP 2.
.B ICLI_*
environment variables;
.IP 3.
.I .icli.toml
in the current directory or the nearest parent (stopping at a
.I .git
directory);
.IP 4.
.IR $IDAUSR/icli.toml ;
.IP 5.
.IR $IDADIR/cfg/icli.toml ;
.IP 6.
built\-in defaults.
.PP
Kernel directives follow IDA's own order
.RI ( $IDADIR/cfg/ida.cfg ,
.IR $IDAUSR/cfg/ida.cfg ,
.IR $IDAUSR/idauser.cfg ),
then the
.B [ida]
and
.B [hexrays]
tables of the
.B icli
files, then
.BR \-\-set .
.PP
.EX
# .icli.toml
[defaults]
format      = "jsonl"
addr        = "rva"
analysis    = "wait"

[load]
compiler    = "visual"
symbols     = ["auto", "symsrv"]

[analyze]
with        = ["lumina", "rtti", "pdb"]

[ida]                       # same as \-\-set
OPCODE_BYTES = 8
ANALYSIS     = "+FLIRT,+HFLIRT,\-UNK"

[hexrays]
MAX_NCOMMAS  = 8

[cache]
dir      = "~/.cache/icli"
max\-size = "50G"

[alias]                     # git\-style
hot   = "list functions \-\-sort callers:desc \-n 20"
fails = "list functions \-\-where \(aqhexrays_err != 0\(aq"
.EE
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B IDADIR
Installation directory (modules, loaders, plugins,
.IR cfg/ ", " sig/ ", " til/ ", " ids/ ).
Default: the directory containing
.BR icli .
.TP
.B IDAUSR
User directories (path list) searched before
.BR IDADIR .
Default
.I ~/.idapro
on Linux and macOS,
.I %APPDATA%\eHex\-Rays\eIDA Pro
on Windows.
.TP
.B IDALOG
Kernel message log (as
.BR \-\-log ).
.TP
.B ICLI_DB
Default target.
.TP
.B ICLI_CACHE_DIR
Database cache.
Default
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/icli ,
.I ~/Library/Caches/icli
on macOS,
.I %LOCALAPPDATA%\eicli
on Windows.
.TP
.BR ICLI_FORMAT ", " ICLI_JOBS
Defaults for
.B \-\-format
and
.BR \-\-jobs .
.TP
.BR ICLI_SOCKET ", " ICLI_NO_SERVER
Use a specific
.B icli serve
socket; or never forward.
.TP
.B ICLI_LAST
Maintained by the shell integration from
.B icli completion
so that a bare
.B @
works.
.TP
.B ICLI_AUTHOR
Author for journal records.
Default: the licence holder, then
.BR $USER .
.TP
.B ICLI_ALLOW_EXECUTE
If
.BR 1 ,
acts as
.BR \-\-allow\-execute .
For sandboxed CI only.
.TP
.B ICLI_DEBUG_PASSWORD
Remote debug server password.
.TP
.BR VAULT_HOST ", " VAULT_USER ", " VAULT_PASS ", " VAULT_SITE
IDA Teams connection, as for
.BR hv (1).
.TP
.BR _NT_SYMBOL_PATH ", " DEBUGINFOD_URLS
Symbol sources for
.BR "\-\-symbols symsrv" / debuginfod .
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colour.
.TP
.B TMPDIR
Temporary databases for
.BR \-\-no\-cache .
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH FILES
.TP
.IR $ICLI_CACHE_DIR/ xx / key .i64
Cached databases.
.TP
.I $ICLI_CACHE_DIR/index.sqlite
Cache index: key, input path and hash, load options, state, sizes, access
times.
.TP
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/icli/ key .sock
.B icli serve
sockets.
.TP
.IR db .i64.lock
Lock file (pid, host, mode).
.TP
.IR $IDAUSR/icli/recipes/ name .icli
Recipes for
.BR "icli do @" \fIname\fP .
.TP
.IR $IDAUSR/icli.toml ", " ./.icli.toml
.B icli
configuration.
.TP
.IR $IDADIR/cfg/ida.cfg ", " $IDADIR/cfg/hexrays.cfg ", " $IDAUSR/idauser.cfg
Kernel and decompiler configuration.
.TP
.IR $IDADIR/sig/ proc /*.sig ", " $IDADIR/til/ proc /*.til ", " $IDADIR/ids/
FLIRT signatures, type libraries, import name databases.
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH EXIT STATUS
Codes are stable across releases.
When several apply, the lowest non\-zero code wins, except that 3 yields to
any hard error.
.TP 6
.B 0
Success.
For edits, also when nothing needed to change.
.TP
.B 1
Negative result:
.BR search ,
.B resolve
or
.B list \-\-where
found nothing;
.B assert
failed;
.B diff
found differences;
.B \-\-dry\-run
edit would change nothing;
.B identify
met an unrecognised file.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: unknown command, option or
.B \-\-set
key; malformed selector; load option conflicting with an existing database;
dynamic command without
.BR \-\-allow\-execute .
.TP
.B 3
Partial: analysis timed out, some functions failed to decompile, some
journal records were skipped.
Output is complete for what succeeded.
.TP
.B 4
Input file not found or unreadable.
.TP
.B 5
A selector the command requires resolved to nothing.
.TP
.B 6
Load failure: no loader accepted the file, or the loader or processor
rejected it.
.TP
.B 7
Licence: no valid licence, or the edition lacks the feature (e.g. the
decompiler for this processor).
.TP
.B 8
Decompilation of a single requested function failed.
.TP
.B 9
Edit conflict: a user\-set value without
.BR \-\-force ,
a name already in use, a differing type definition.
.TP
.B 10
Timeout (debugger, server, or
.B \-\-analysis\-timeout
under
.BR \-\-strict ).
.TP
.B 11
Database locked by another process.
.TP
.B 12
Database below the required lifecycle state with
.BR \-\-analysis=none .
.TP
.B 13
Write attempted on a read\-only database.
.TP
.B 14
Database corrupt, or created by a newer IDA.
.TP
.B 15
Network error (Lumina, IDA Teams, symbol server, remote debugger).
.TP
.B 16
Script error: uncaught exception in
.BR exec .
Code calling
.BI qexit( n )
exits with
.I n
instead.
.TP
.B 70
Internal error (INTERR).
The number is printed; the database is not saved.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted.
The database is saved consistent; analysis resumes next time.
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS First contact
Decompile
.B main
of a file never seen before.
It is loaded, analysed and cached; the second run takes milliseconds:
.PP
.EX
$ icli decompile ./crackme main
.EE
.PP
Triage a directory without creating any database:
.PP
.EX
$ icli identify samples/* \e
      \-t \(aq{sha256:.16}  {arch:<10} {compiler:<14} {packer} {path}\(aq
.EE
.PP
What would IDA do with this blob?
.PP
.EX
$ icli loaders mystery.img
.EE
.PP
Raw Cortex\-M firmware with SRAM, a peripheral map, and a summary as JSON:
.PP
.EX
$ icli info \-f json \-\-processor arm:ARMv7\-M \-\-base 0x08000000 \e
      \-\-segment SRAM=0x20000000\-0x20020000:DATA:rw \e
      \-\-svd STM32F407.svd fw.bin | jq .
.EE
.PP
Fully enriched analysis with a time budget, in CI:
.PP
.EX
$ icli \-q \-\-analysis\-timeout 20m analyze \e
      \-\-with lumina,pdb,rtti,findmain app.exe
$ echo $?           # 0 complete, 3 partial
.EE
.PP
One library out of a dyld shared cache; one dex out of an APK:
.PP
.EX
$ icli list exports dyld_shared_cache_arm64e::libsystem_kernel.dylib
$ icli decompile \-\-all app.apk::classes2.dex \(aqfunc:/^Lcom\e/example\e//\(aq
.EE
.SS Querying
The 20 largest non\-library functions, as a table:
.PP
.EX
$ icli list functions \-\-where \(aq!lib\(aq \-\-sort size:desc \-n 20 \e
      \-t \(aq{ea}  {size:>8}  {xrefs_to:>4}  {demangled}\(aq app.exe
.EE
.PP
Functions that both receive network data and call
.BR memcpy :
.PP
.EX
$ icli resolve app.exe \(aqcallers*(imp:*!recv) & callers(imp:*!memcpy)\(aq
.EE
.PP
Every call site of
.BR system ,
with the decompiled line:
.PP
.EX
$ icli xrefs \-\-type call app.exe \(aqimp:*!system\(aq \e
  | icli decompile \-\-at\-line app.exe \-
.EE
.PP
Strings that look like URLs and who uses them:
.PP
.EX
$ icli search \-\-string \(aq^https?://\(aq app.exe \e
  | jq \-r \(aq[.value, (.funcs | join(","))] | @tsv\(aq
.EE
.PP
Known crypto constants and the functions referencing them:
.PP
.EX
$ icli search \-\-crypto \-t \(aq{ea} {name:<20} {refs}\(aq app.exe
.EE
.PP
Imports from crypto DLLs as CSV:
.PP
.EX
$ icli \-f csv list imports app.exe \e
      \-\-where \(aqmodule ~ "(?i)bcrypt|advapi32"\(aq
.EE
.PP
Call graph of the network layer:
.PP
.EX
$ icli callgraph \-\-callees \-\-depth 3 \-\-graph dot app.exe net_dispatch \e
  | dot \-Tsvg > net.svg
.EE
.SS Editing
Rename every remaining dummy function after its body hash, so names stay
stable across rebuilds; preview first:
.PP
.EX
$ icli \-\-dry\-run rename app.exe \(aqfunc:*[dummy]\(aq \(aqf_{hash:.8}\(aq
$ icli rename app.exe \(aqfunc:*[dummy]\(aq \(aqf_{hash:.8}\(aq     # again: no\-op
.EE
.PP
Retype all dispatch routines and let the types propagate:
.PP
.EX
$ icli type set \-\-propagate drv.sys \(aqfunc:Dispatch*\(aq \e
      \(aqNTSTATUS __stdcall {name}(PDEVICE_OBJECT, PIRP)\(aq
.EE
.PP
Import a header, then apply a prototype:
.PP
.EX
$ icli type add app.exe \-I ./include proto.h
$ icli type set app.exe 0x401230 \(aqint parse_packet(pkt_t *p, size_t n)\(aq
.EE
.PP
Bulk rename from another tool's output:
.PP
.EX
$ cut \-f1,2 matches.tsv | icli rename app.i64 \-
.EE
.PP
Tag everything within three calls of CryptoAPI:
.PP
.EX
$ icli tag \-\-color ffe0e0 mal.exe \(aqcallers(imp:advapi32!Crypt*, 3)\(aq crypto
.EE
.PP
Patch a branch and write both a DIF and the patched file:
.PP
.EX
$ icli patch asm app.exe \(aqcheck_update+0x1c\(aq \(aqjmp short loc_skip\(aq
$ icli export dif \-o app.dif app.exe
$ icli export exe \-o app.patched.exe app.exe
.EE
.PP
Review the week's changes and undo a mistake:
.PP
.EX
$ icli log \-\-since 7d \-f text app.i64
$ icli undo \-\-to 412 app.i64
.EE
.SS The edit loop
Lumina proposals, filtered by confidence, reviewed, applied:
.PP
.EX
$ icli lumina pull app.exe \e
  | jq \-c \(aqselect(.score >= 0.9)\(aq \e
  | icli apply \-\-only rename,type app.exe \-
.EE
.PP
Keep annotations in git rather than in a binary database:
.PP
.EX
$ icli export journal \-o app.journal.jsonl app.exe
$ git add app.journal.jsonl && git commit \-m "annotations"
# elsewhere, same input:
$ icli apply app.exe app.journal.jsonl
.EE
.PP
Carry all names, types and comments from 1.2 to 1.3:
.PP
.EX
$ icli port \-\-what names,types,comments app\-1.2.i64 app\-1.3.exe
.EE
.SS Decompiler
Everything into one compilable\-looking C file, 16 threads:
.PP
.EX
$ icli \-j 16 export c \-o app.c app.exe
.EE
.PP
One file per user function:
.PP
.EX
$ icli export c \-o \(aqsrc/{name}.c\(aq app.exe \(aqfunc:*[!lib && !thunk]\(aq
.EE
.PP
Which functions fail to decompile, and why:
.PP
.EX
$ icli list functions \-\-where \(aqhexrays_err != 0\(aq \e
      \-t \(aq{ea} {name} err={hexrays_err}\(aq app.exe
.EE
.PP
Microcode before and after global optimisation, ready to diff:
.PP
.EX
$ icli do app.exe \-\- \e
      export mc \-\-maturity locopt \-o pre.mc  parse_hdr :: \e
      export mc \-\-maturity lvars  \-o post.mc parse_hdr
$ diff \-u pre.mc post.mc
.EE
.PP
A minimal database reproducing a decompiler bug, to attach to a report:
.PP
.EX
$ icli export i64 \-o repro.i64 big.i64 sub_7ff6a0
.EE
.SS Signatures and types
Build FLIRT signatures for a static library, then use them:
.PP
.EX
$ icli sig make \-\-library\-name "mbedTLS 3.5 x64" \-\-collisions skip \e
      \-o mbedtls35.sig libmbedcrypto.a libmbedtls.a
$ icli sig apply fw.i64 ./mbedtls35.sig
.EE
.PP
A type library from an SDK:
.PP
.EX
$ icli til make \-\-target x86_64\-pc\-windows\-msvc \-I sdk/inc \e
      \-o vendor.til sdk/inc/vendor.h
.EE
.SS Diffing
Patch Tuesday: changed functions with a pseudocode diff:
.PP
.EX
$ icli \-j 16 diff \-\-pseudocode \-\-threshold 0.5 \e
      old/ntoskrnl.exe new/ntoskrnl.exe \e
  | jq \-r \(aqselect(.diff == "changed") | .patch\(aq | less \-R
.EE
.PP
Sorted by similarity, as a table:
.PP
.EX
$ icli diff \-t \(aq{similarity:.3f}  {ea} <\- {other_ea}  {name}\(aq \e
      old.i64 new.i64 | sort \-n | head
.EE
.SS Pipelines, chains and CI
One load, many outputs:
.PP
.EX
$ icli do kernel.elf \-\- \e
      sig apply auto :: \e
      analyze \-\-with rtti :: \e
      export lst \-o kernel.lst :: \e
      export map \-o kernel.map :: \e
      export c   \-o kernel.c   :: \e
      export h   \-o kernel.h
.EE
.PP
A chain where each step feeds the next through
.BR % :
.PP
.EX
$ icli do mal.exe \-\- \e
      search \-\-crypto :: \e
      tag % crypto :: \e
      export c \-o crypto.c \(aqfunc(%)\(aq
.EE
.PP
A reusable recipe,
.IR $IDAUSR/icli/recipes/win\-triage.icli :
.PP
.EX
sig apply auto
analyze \-\-with rtti,findmain
export sarif \-o {input}.sarif \(aqcallers(imp:*!strcpy | imp:*!sprintf)\(aq
export journal \-o {input}.journal.jsonl
.EE
.PP
.EX
$ icli do sample.exe @win\-triage
.EE
.PP
Fail a CI job if more than three functions stop decompiling:
.PP
.EX
$ icli assert app.exe \(aqfunc:*[hexrays_err != 0]\(aq \(aq<= 3\(aq
.EE
.PP
Triage a corpus in parallel:
.PP
.EX
$ find samples/ \-type f \-print0 \e
  | xargs \-0 \-P 8 \-n 1 icli \-q \-\-analysis\-timeout 5m info > triage.jsonl
.EE
.PP
Thousands of small queries against one hot database:
.PP
.EX
$ icli serve \-\-detach \-\-idle\-timeout 2h kernel.i64
$ time icli list functions \-\-count kernel.i64     # ~10 ms
.EE
.PP
Load everything into SQLite:
.PP
.EX
$ icli export sqlite \-o app.db app.exe
$ sqlite3 app.db \(aqSELECT name, size FROM functions WHERE callers = 0\(aq
.EE
.PP
Run a Python file and propagate its verdict:
.PP
.EX
$ icli exec app.exe find_bugs.py \-\- \-\-min\-score 7 \e
  || echo "findings: $?"
.EE
.SS Python
Look up the API:
.PP
.EX
$ icli ref "rename local variable"
.EE
.PP
A command that almost does what you want, as code to adapt:
.PP
.EX
$ icli list functions \-\-where \(aqsize > 0x400\(aq \-\-show\-code app.exe
for f in db.functions:
    if f.size > 0x400:
        yield {"ea": f.start_ea, "name": db.functions.get_name(f),
               "size": f.size}
.EE
.PP
A one\-off query whose result is ordinary records:
.PP
.EX
$ icli exec app.exe \-c \(aq[{"ea": f.start_ea,
                          "name": db.functions.get_name(f)}
                         for f in db.functions if f.size > 0x1000]\(aq \e
  | jq \-r .name
.EE
.PP
Code proposes names; review them; apply them (journaled, undoable):
.PP
.EX
$ icli exec app.exe guess_names.py > proposals.jsonl
$ jq \-c \(aqselect(.confidence > 0.8)\(aq proposals.jsonl | icli apply app.exe \-
.EE
.PP
Per\-item code over a selection:
.PP
.EX
$ icli exec app.exe \-\-each \(aqfunc:*[!lib]\(aq \e
      \-c \(aq{"ea": ea, "loops": count_loops(db, ea)}\(aq
.EE
.PP
A persistent session, also served over MCP:
.PP
.EX
$ icli serve \-\-detach \-\-mcp http:127.0.0.1:8737 app.i64
$ icli exec app.i64 \-\-session work \-c \(aqimport networkx as nx\(aq
$ icli exec app.i64 \-\-session work \-c \(aqg = build_cfg(db, "main")\(aq
$ icli exec app.i64 \-\-session work \-c \(aqnx.dag_longest_path_length(g)\(aq
.EE
.SS Dynamic
Code coverage from a test run, highlighted in a listing:
.PP
.EX
$ icli \-\-allow\-execute trace \-\-coverage app.exe \e
      \-\- tests/input1 > cov.jsonl
$ icli export html \-\-highlight cov.jsonl \-o cov.html app.exe
$ icli list functions \-\-where \(aqcoverage == 0\(aq app.exe \(aqfunc:parse*\(aq
.EE
.PP
Log the arguments of a function on every call:
.PP
.EX
$ icli \-\-allow\-execute debug run \-\-break parse_packet \-\-regs rcx,rdx \e
      \-\-timeout 60s app.exe \-\- \-\-port 8080
.EE
.SS Teams
.PP
.EX
$ icli rename vault://corp/router/router.i64 0x8001_2340 nvram_get
$ icli vault commit \-m "named nvram accessors" \e
      vault://corp/router/router.i64
.EE
