.TE
.SS Stability
Command and option names, exit codes, and the field names of
.BR json ", " jsonl ", " csv ", " tsv
output are the stable interface.
Fields may be added in minor releases; a field is never removed or renamed
without a schema version bump, and the previous schema stays available via
.B \-\-schema\-version
for one major release.
.B text
output carries no guarantee.
.SS Determinism
With the same input, IDA version, load options and configuration, analysis
is deterministic: two cold runs produce byte\-identical
.B list
output.
.B \-j
never changes results.
Lumina pulls and symbol downloads are not deterministic; they are recorded
in the journal so that
.B icli apply
reproduces them offline.
.SS Security
Loading untrusted input is analysis, not execution.
Nothing runs the target without
.BR \-\-allow\-execute ;
scripts stored in databases are never run automatically; loader plugins
from
.B IDAUSR
are honoured, so do not point
.B IDAUSR
at untrusted directories.
.SS Performance
Opening a multi\-gigabyte database costs seconds; a served database answers
in milliseconds.
Scripts issuing more than a handful of commands against one database should
use
.BR "icli serve" ,
.BR "icli do" ,
.BR "icli batch" ,
or
.BR "icli exec \-\-session" .
.SS Editions
.B icli
requires IDA Pro or IDA Home with idalib.
Decompilation requires the corresponding decompiler licence.
Lumina push, IDA Teams and remote debugging follow the edition's terms.
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH BUGS
The cache key covers the input and load options, not external files read
during analysis (PDB, separate DWARF, Lumina).
Run
.B analyze \-\-reanalyze
after they change.
.PP
Fields that need the decompiler
.RB ( pseudocode ,
.BR hexrays_err )
in a predicate or template silently decompile; an innocent
.B list
can become very slow.
.PP
Structural matching in
.B diff
is quadratic in the number of functions left unmatched by the cheaper
rounds; very large, heavily changed binaries can take minutes.
.PP
.B patch asm
is only as good as the processor module's assembler; most non\-x86/ARM
modules have none and the command exits 2.
.PP
Per\-item
.B \-o
templates sanitise file names, so two C++ overloads may collide; use
.B \(aq{name}_{ea}.c\(aq
when in doubt.
.PP
Report bugs with the output of
.B "icli \-vv \-\-version"
and, when possible,
.BR "icli export i64" " of the affected function and " "icli export journal" .
